# Template for secrets/local.env (gitignored — copy this file there and fill it in).
#
# This is the ONLY secret docker-compose needs to inject directly: the token to
# reach Vault in the first place. Everything else (DB, Mongo, mail, OAuth, Kafka
# SASL, etc.) is resolved from Vault's own KV store once bootstrap succeeds — it
# never belongs in this file, in config/local.env, or in a Helm values file.
#
# In Kubernetes, prefer Vault's Kubernetes auth method (the pod's ServiceAccount
# authenticates to Vault directly) over a static token like this one, so there's
# no token to provision, rotate, or leak via a Secret/values file at all.

VAULT_TOKEN=
